\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 02 \'b7 The Problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Asset: 02.mov\
Boards was under development, and Raspberry had scoped the build. Every tool in the classic app needed a canvas equivalent. Multi-material masking in Sketch to Render was still missing.\
Masking is where a designer makes decisions worth comparing. This fabric on the collar, that one on the sleeve, up to three at once. In the classic app it happened in a modal: a window that takes over the screen, does its job, and hands you back.\
A modal would have worked anywhere else but Boards exists so a designer can compare options and reference existing designs. Masking is exactly when they'd want to check and a modal on top puts the board out of reach.\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 03 \'b7 Constraints\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 A toolset built for a modal.
\f1\b0  Masking already had three selection tools (smart mask, lasso, brush) each with its own controls, laid out for a modal.\

\f0\b Two navigation systems on the same gestures.
\f1\b0  The masking tool and the canvas each have their own pan and zoom.\

\f0\b Platform rules I couldn't change.
\f1\b0  Up to three materials, each masked separately, and nothing to generate without a masked area for each.\

\f0\b Boards was still being built while I designed against it.
\f1\b0  The surface I was adding to was still changing.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 04 \'b7 The Decisions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1 \'97 Mask in place, not in a modal\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Asset: 04-1-1.png; 04-1-2.png\
Porting the modal on top of the canvas was the safe option: proven, focused, with room for every control.\
I made masking a mode instead. Uploading a material image and entering masking mode focuses the image and raises a toolbar carrying both selection tools and materials. The canvas stays visible behind it.\
The reason is the same one that justifies creating Boards: masking is where a designer decides what differentiates one option from others on the canvas. A modal preserves the work underneath, but it makes every check deliberate (close it, look, reopen) and what costs a click gets consulted less.\
Asset: 04-1-3.png\
Moving onto the canvas traded space for navigation. A modal has room for every control, a floating toolbar doesn't, so selection tools nest in a dropdown and switching costs an extra click. The canvas already pans and zooms so masking's navigation came off the toolbar entirely, combining two systems into one, a simplification the modal couldn't make.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2 \'97 Let designers leave mid-mask\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Asset: 04-2.png\
Using the canvas's navigation raised a new question: does it stay live while masking?\
Locking it would have been safer, but a frozen canvas recreates the modal's problem in a different shape \'97 the board visible, still unreachable. A designer masking a collar might want to compare with a previous version or another colourway. There's little point moving masking onto the canvas if it stops working the moment you use it.\
The cost is now a designer can navigate away from the image mid-edit. The toolbar anchors to the image rather than the viewport, tracking its position, holding its size as the canvas zooms, and if someone leaves it behind entirely, a snackbar offers to take them back.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 05 \'b7 Craft & System\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 The node does three jobs
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Asset: 05-1.png\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
It holds up to three materials, mirrored from the toolbar, visible even when masking is closed, tracking state and letting a click reopen masking directly.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
It also gates generation, disabled until every material is masked, with a running count (e.g. 1/3 materials masked) showing what's outstanding.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Anchored to the image
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Asset: 05-2.png\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The toolbar anchors to the image, following pans and holding size through zooms, so it's never a four-pixel strip or oversized slab.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Five controls, two exits
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Asset: 05-3.mov\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Undo, redo, save, reset, and close. Two exits: save then leave, or leave without saving.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Interrupted, not cancelled
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Asset: 05-4.png\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Panning away doesn't end masking. A snackbar keeps the mask open, offering a route back or an exit.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Accessibility
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The snackbar has no timer. It\'92s a status indicator, not a notification, so it stays until resolved. A self-dismissing one fails whoever takes longest to reach it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
